.TH AVR\-SERVICE\-TOKEN\-REVOKE 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-service-token-revoke \- Revoke a service token.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr service-token revoke
[OPTIONS] TOKEN_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Revoke a service token.
.PP
Its current secret and any old secret still in its rotation overlap stop working on their next request, and its grants are removed. Revoking a token that is already revoked succeeds.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr service-token revoke <token-id>
    avr service-token revoke <token-id> --yes
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fITOKEN_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR, \fB\-y\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-service-token (1),
.BR avr-service-token-create (1),
.BR avr-service-token-list (1),
.BR avr-service-token-revoke-all (1),
.BR avr-service-token-rotate (1),
.BR avr-service-token-set-access (1),
.BR avr-service-token-view (1)
